  "id": "two-relays-a-flapping-relay-does-not-stall-setup",
  "description": "One relay accepts connections and drops them again every two seconds while the other works. Losing one mailbox must not reset the setup while another one reaches the peer: the parent's request for an offer stays valid, the baby answers it, and the attempt verifies in seconds instead of after the 20 s attempt timeout, with one attempt per side.",
